Whitecourt, Alta – On Feb. 20, 2026, the Alberta
RCMP
’s Community Response Team, with the assistance from the Whitecourt
RCMP
and Western Alberta Crime Reduction Unit, executed a search warrant on a residence and vehicle on 47 Street in Whitecourt. As a result of the search warrant, police located and seized:
370 grams of methamphetamine;
5 grams of cocaine;
62 grams of cannabis;
1 gram of ketamine;
400mL of GHB;
51 unknown pills;
Extendable baton;
Imitation firearm;
Drug-trafficking paraphernalia; and
$915 in Canadian currency.
As a result of the investigation, a 43-year-old resident of Whitecourt, was charged with:
Possession for the purpose of trafficking (x7);
Possession of a weapon dangerous to the public (x2); and
Possession of proceeds of crime under $5000.
The individual was brought before a justice of the peace and remanded into custody. They are to appear before the Alberta Court of Justice in Whitecourt on March 10, 2026.
