RM of South Cypress-Glenboro, Manitoba
From: Manitoba RCMP
The Manitoba RCMP Roving Traffic Unit seized drugs and a weapon following a traffic stop on Feb. 14.
On February 14, at approximately 11 :15 p.m., the Manitoba
RCMP
Roving Traffic Unit initiated a traffic stop that resulted in two arrests after drugs and a loaded handgun were found inside the vehicle.
RCMP
officers pulled a vehicle over with two individuals inside on Highway 2 within the RM of South Cypress-Glenboro. During the interaction with the vehicle occupants, an officer noted a controlled substance in plain sight, along with a prohibited weapon.
The suspects were arrested as a result.
A subsequent search of the vehicle netted a loaded handgun, two kilograms of a substance believed to be cocaine, several grams of a substance believed to be methamphetamine and additional prohibited weapons.
Tyler Thorvaldson, 29, of Carman, and Kyle Tkachyk, 43, of Elm Creek have been charged with:
Possession for the purpose of trafficking cocaine;
Possession of methamphetamine;
Unauthorized possession of a prohibited weapon;
Possession of a prohibited weapon without a licence;
Possession of a firearm in a motor vehicle;
Possession of a loaded prohibited weapon in a motor vehicle;
Possession of a weapon for a dangerous purpose;
Unsafe storage of a firearm; and
Careless use of a firearm.
Thorvaldson was also ticketed for driving a vehicle equipped with a radar detection device and carrying open liquor inside a vehicle.
Both were remanded into custody.

Swan River, Manitoba
From: Manitoba RCMP
A 37-year-old male wanted in connection with a head-on collision that killed three people on July 1, 2025, has been arrested.
Matthew Govereau was taken into custody on Feb. 14 by Winnipeg Police Service officers. Govereau was arrested in Winnipeg.
The July 1 collision saw a vehicle veer over the centre line of Highway 10 north of Swan River and hit a parked vehicle. A 42-year-old male and a 31-year-old female who were in the parked vehicle died of their injuries, as did a 29-year-old passenger in the moving vehicle.
Govereau has been charged with 18 offences relating to the July 1 crash. The charges include:
Impaired driving causing death x3;
Dangerous operation of a vehicle causing death x3;
Careless driving x3;
Possession of a weapon for a dangerous purpose;
Possessing a prohibited weapon;
Weapon possession contrary to order x2;
Possession of property obtained by crime;
Possession of drugs for purposes of trafficking x3; and
Possession of a controlled substance.
Govereau has been remanded into custody and is scheduled to make a court appearance on Tuesday in Winnipeg.
The
RCMP
thanks both the public and the Winnipeg Police Service for their assistance.

Two people have been charged after a shooting took place in North Battleford, SK on February 8, 2026.
On February 8, 2026, around 9:30 p.m., Battlefords
RCMP
received a report of shots being fired at a residential building in North Battleford, Saskatchewan. Officers immediately responded and confirmed there were no injuries. Further investigation determined the suspects fled the scene in a grey SUV.
Battlefords
RCMP
were conducting extensive patrols and located the vehicle matching the description driving on Highway 16. Officers attempted stop the vehicle, however the vehicle continued to proceed down the highway. Officers continued to follow the vehicle at a high rate of speed, when it then turned down a rural road. Eventually the vehicle came to a sudden stop.
RCMP
officers and Saskatchewan
RCMP
’s Police Dog Services contained the vehicle. Two suspects were observed in the vehicle. The one suspect exited the vehicle, threw a firearm on the ground and re-entered the vehicle.
After multiple requests to exit the vehicle, the two male suspects exited the vehicle and were arrested without incident. Officers at the scene seized the loaded firearm that had earlier been thrown on the ground.  In a further search of the vehicle, officers located firearm ammunition and bear spray.
32-year-old Monty Bear from Little Pine First Nation, SK, is charged with:
one count, discharge firearm while being reckless, Section 244.2(3), Criminal Code;
one count, flight from police, Section 320.17 of the Criminal Code;
one count, dangerous operation of a motor vehicle, Section 320.13(1) of the Criminal Code;
one count, possession of restricted firearm/prohibited weapon with ammunition without license/registration, Section 95(1), Criminal Code;
one count, possession of a firearm in a motor vehicle, Section 94(1), Criminal Code;
one count, operation while prohibited, Section 320.18, Criminal Code;
two counts, fail to comply probation order, Section 733.1(1), Criminal Code;
one count, weapons/firearms possession contrary to order, Section 117.01(1), Criminal Code;
one count, possession of a weapon for a dangerous purpose, Section 88(1), Criminal Code; and
one count, operation while impaired of motor vehicle, Section 320.14(1)(a), Criminal Code.
Monty Bear appeared in North Battleford Provincial Court on February 10, 2026.
29-year-old Blake Kasokeo from Poundmaker First Nation, SK is charged with:
one count, discharge firearm while being reckless, Section 244.2(3), Criminal Code;
one count, possession of restricted firearm/prohibited weapon with ammunition without license/registration, Section 95(1), Criminal Code;
one count, possession of a firearm in a motor vehicle, Section 94(1), Criminal Code;
one count, weapons/firearms possession contrary to order, Section 117.01(1), Criminal Code; and
one count, possession of a weapon for a dangerous purpose, Section 88(1), Criminal Code.
Blake Kasokeo appeared in North Battleford Provincial Court on February 10, 2026.
