Swan Hills, Alta.
-
On Jan. 22, 2026, members of the Western Alberta District
RCMP
Crime Reduction Unit (WADCRU) with assistance from the Swan Hills detachment, Western Alberta District General Investigative Services and the K Division Auto Theft Unit executed a criminal code search warrant on multiple locations in Swan Hills. The multi-month investigation was centered around stolen vehicles, the alteration of vehicle identification numbers, and the fraudulent trafficking of stolen vehicles to unsuspecting victims.
As a result of the search and broader investigation police recovered;
Multiple stolen vehicles with value over $5000, including a pick-up truck, trailer, Harley-Davidson motorcycle, snowmobiles, and other off highway vehicles;
Three firearms, including one prohibited, a crossbow, and ammunition;
Approximately 10 grams of methamphetamine; and
Additional offence related property.
Five individuals were arrested and charged,
First individual, a 33-year-old resident of Swan Hills with;
Fraud greater than $5000;
Fraud under $5000 (x2);
Trafficking in property obtained by crime over $5000;
Alter/Destroy/Remove a Vehicle Identification Number (x3);
Forgery (x2); and
Use/Traffic/Possess a forged document.
Second individual, a 32-year-old resident of Swan Hills, with;
Fraud greater than $5000;
Fraud under $5000;
Trafficking in property obtained by crime over $5000;
Alter/Destroy/Remove a Vehicle Identification Number (x2); and
Use/Traffic/Possess a forged document.
Third individual, a 63-year-old resident of Swan Hills with;
Possession of property obtained by crime over $5000 (x4); and
Alter/Destroy/Remove a Vehicle Identification Number (x3).
Fourth individual, a 35-year-old resident of Swan Hills, with;
Alter/Destroy/Remove a Vehicle Identification Number;
Fraud under $5000;
Possession of property obtained by crime over $5000 (x3);
Possession of a prohibited weapon when knowing unauthorized;
Unauthorized possession of a firearm (x2);
Unsafe storage of firearms (x3);
Possession of prohibited firearm with readily accessible ammunition; and
Use/Traffic/Possess a forged document.
Fifth individual, a 35-year-old resident Swan Hills, with;
Possession of property obtained by crime over $5000 (x2);
Possession of a prohibited weapon when knowing unauthorized;
Unauthorized possession of a firearm (x2);
Unsafe storage of firearms (x3); and
Possession of prohibited firearm with readily accessible ammunition.
“This is a great example of an
RCMP
multi-unit collaboration, bringing together local knowledge, district-level resources and specialized expertise to effectively dismantle this operation. Improving public safety through the removal of stolen vehicles, firearms, and drugs remains a key focus for our unit”. says Cst. Dylan Macleod, primary investigator assigned to the case. The
RCMP
reminds the public to exercise caution when purchasing used vehicles and recreational equipment.
The second, third and fifth individuals, were released before an officer in charge with a scheduled court appearance of March 24, 2026, at the Alberta Court of Justice in Barrhead. The first individual was brought before a Justice of the Peace and released from custody with a next court appearance of Feb. 10, 2026, at the Alberta Court of Justice in Barrhead. The forth individual was also brought before a Justice of the Peace and was remanded into custody with their next court appearance scheduled for Jan. 27, 2026, at the Alberta Court of Justice in Barrhead.
